288
00:17:32,713 --> 00:17:36,423
And this is cool because it means
that you can use any type of

289
00:17:36,503 --> 00:17:41,873
LLM that you so desire alongside
Gigapipe, and it will work great.

290
00:17:41,933 --> 00:17:46,834
And the reason is since our storage
layer is unified and you have all the

291
00:17:46,834 --> 00:17:51,544
signals inside of it natively correlated,
it means that your LLM integrations,

292
00:17:51,703 --> 00:17:56,614
MCP servers, your agentic workflows
will be able to reason in real-time

293
00:17:56,653 --> 00:18:00,474
without giving timeouts, without
returning nonsenti-nonsensical replies.

